---
title: Service runbook
description: Give an operator the correct commands and escalation contact for a service.
schema:
  Systemd:
    kind: "'systemd'"
    host: string
    unit: string
  Local:
    kind: "'local'"
    directory: string
    command: string
  Check:
    name: string
    url: string.url
    expected: string
  Contact:
    team: string
    channel: string
  Runbook:
    name: string
    purpose: string
    deployment: Systemd | Local
    checks: Check[]
    onCall: Contact
input: Runbook
---
# {name}

{purpose}

## Start and stop

<$match value={deployment}>
  <$case type="Systemd">
    Unit: `{deployment.unit}` on `{deployment.host}`.

    ```sh
    ssh "{deployment.host}" 'systemctl --user start "{deployment.unit}"'
    ssh "{deployment.host}" 'systemctl --user status "{deployment.unit}"'
    ssh "{deployment.host}" 'systemctl --user stop "{deployment.unit}"'
    ```

    Inspect recent logs before restarting a failing service:

    ```sh
    ssh "{deployment.host}" 'journalctl --user -u "{deployment.unit}" -n 100 --no-pager'
    ```
  </$case>
  <$case type="Local">
    Run from `{deployment.directory}`:

    ```sh
    cd "{deployment.directory}"
    {deployment.command}
    ```

    Stop the process with Ctrl+C in the terminal that started it.
  </$case>
</$match>

## Health checks

<$each items={checks} as="check">
  ### {check.name}

  ```sh
  curl --fail --silent --show-error "{check.url}"
  ```

  Expected: {check.expected}

</$each>
<$include src="./shared/escalation.mdt" with={{serviceName: name, contact: onCall}} />
